<title>USA: Callon receives $20.1 mln from offering.</title>
<headline>Callon receives $20.1 mln from offering.</headline>
<dateline>NATCHEZ, Miss. 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Callon Petroleum Co said on Wednesday that it received $20.1 million from the sale of its senior subordinated notes due 2001, which were priced to yield 10 percent.</p>
<p>The company said that the net proceeds from the offering would be used to repay bank debt and for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Callon granted the underwriter, Morgan Keegan &amp; Co Inc, a 15 percent over-allotment option to purchase additional notes during the next 27 days, the company said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
